{"kind":"assert","text":"Review note for Hugh: derive request labels from the signed reference, and stop maintaining them again in handoff prose.\n\nA small history trap illustrates the cost. [#15915 is event addressing](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A5da1e08bdbdf3e0ff2c211b560325a865ecb6eae); [#15916 is the notification dropdown](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A59e582a8edb2ab2b5b11f24123d064cf31c131bf). The [addressing promise](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A1844762b9ffafeb686d4699b8b52ad0a488c3aeb) calls its request #15916, and the [notification promise](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3A1265afe91305ae5340d10c1eec353c31f9b42f4b) calls its request #15915. The [notification implementation report](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3Abae33e6e9ff9f1d2e138724c5f52763383b7132d) repeats #15915. A reader following those numbers reaches the other task. Yet both promises rest on the right canonical requests, the notification commit trailer names the right request, and both outcomes are satisfied with incorporated merge receipts. This is a communication error, not lost work or a reason to reopen either feature. [Checked evidence](request-label-evidence.json).\n\nMy recommendation is a small extension of the concise-primary-report guidance in #19016: show one request reference with its actual number and short title, linked by canonical event ID; generate that label from the same verified projection that supplies the reference. Keep the rest of the report about the result and evidence. Path companions need not copy the request number yet again. This preserves short, readable numbers while giving them one source of truth.\n\nThe [existing reference renderer](ui/src/components/RecordDetail.tsx@e8278a6dacd14b08bbbcd1276fc193edd6401f53:175) already demonstrates the rule: its event determines its label and destination. Reuse that approach in generated handoffs rather than adding a prose parser, another admission check, or a new workflow state. A compact fixture with these two neighboring requests and swapped prose labels is enough to check that the generated reference still names the correct task. Historical signed wording stays intact; structured provenance remains the authority.\n\nPilot this as a writing convention in the next few handoffs: one canonical request link, its current number/title, and no repeated manually copied identity labels. #21309 is already implementing convenient #N/hash input resolution; it should continue its agreed scope and leave free prose alone. Any later handoff helper can use that shared lookup instead of creating a second resolver. This note is for your review, not a new implementation assignment or an added gate.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1265afe91305ae5340d10c1eec353c31f9b42f4b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1844762b9ffafeb686d4699b8b52ad0a488c3aeb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:59e582a8edb2ab2b5b11f24123d064cf31c131bf, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5da1e08bdbdf3e0ff2c211b560325a865ecb6eae, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bae33e6e9ff9f1d2e138724c5f52763383b7132d stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:eb054acb917fe2c9225b0b22414e24010196eb09"}}